        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0649" n="619" xml:id="pg619"/>

                <head>165. Letter From Acting Secretary of State Herter to the President’s Special
                    Assistant for Science and Technology (Killian)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d165-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-08-05">August 5,
                    1958</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Jim</hi>: We are giving urgent consideration to
                    the course of action the United States should take following the present Geneva
                    talks.</p>
                <p>I am sending you with this note a suggested revision of our policy on nuclear
                    testing, which Mr. Dulles has generally approved. For your personal information,
                    I am enclosing also a copy of the staff paper which summarizes briefly our
                    reasons for favoring this course of action rather than a limited test moratorium
                    which Phil Farley tells me John McCone has discussed with you.</p>
                <p>I would welcome a chance to hear your views as to the proper course of action and
                    your comments on our proposal.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Chris</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d165-a1.xml" xpointer="d165-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d165-a2.xml" xpointer="d165-a2"/>
